1
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:08,830
How heavy is this glass of water?

2
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:10,470
Melissa, would you care to answer?

3
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:11,150
Um,

4
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,150
8 oz.

5
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:14,790
12 oz.

6
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,030
16 oz.

7
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:20,870
The absolute weight

8
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:22,510
of the glass doesn't matter.

9
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:24,950
Depends on how long I hold onto it.

10
00:00:25,830 --> 00:00:27,230
If I hold it for a minute, nothing

11
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:27,830
happens.

12
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:29,870
If I hold it for an hour, my arm will

13
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:30,790
begin to ache.

14
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:33,750
If I hold it all day long, my arm will

15
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:35,510
feel numb and paralyzed.

16
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:37,670
Well, the way that the glass hasn't

17
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:39,350
changed, but the longer I hold on to it,

18
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,710
the heavier it becomes.

19
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,230
The stresses and the worries of life are

20
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:45,630
like this glass of water.

21
00:00:46,390 --> 00:00:47,710
If you think about them for a little

22
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:48,870
while, there's no problem.

23
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,950
Think about it for a little bit longer,

24
00:00:52,390 --> 00:00:53,350
it begins to hurt.

25
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:57,070
You think about them all day long, and

26
00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:59,350
you'll feel paralyzed, incapable of doing

27
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:00,150
anything.

28
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:03,030
Always remember

29
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:05,190
put the glass down.

